  $ rtk proxy node --check web/static/js/charts.js  -> SYNTAX OK
  Behavioural: no JS test harness exists in the repo, so I loaded charts.js
  into a node vm sandbox (stubbed Plotly/document) and captured the traces
  handed to Plotly.newPlot. Input values [5,0.5,-0.5,-5,1,-1,1.5,-1.5]:
    A) balance, no neutralBand:  red y=[0,0,-0.5,-5,0,-1,0,-1.5]
                                 green y=[5,0.5,0,0,1,0,1.5,0]   (old behaviour preserved)
    B) balance, neutralBand=1:   red y=[0,0,0,-5,0,0,0,-1.5]
                                 green y=[5,0,0,0,0,0,1.5,0]
       -> 0.5, -0.5, 1, -1 all excluded from BOTH fills; |v| == 1 is excluded,
          matching the card's strict `delta > eps` / `delta < -eps`. 1.5/-1.5
          still filled. Main line trace y = full unclamped values; layout
          shapes y0 = 0 (zero baseline unchanged).
    C) neutralBand=NaN:          identical to A (isFinite guard works)
    D) target mode with neutralBand also passed: 5 traces, y0=10, byte-for-byte
       the old target structure — neutralBand ignored. Target mode untouched.
    E) plain mode: single tozeroy trace, no shapes. Untouched.
    F) initSparklines on an element with data-neutral-band="1":
       red y=[0,0,0,-5], green y=[5,0,0,0]  -> attr reaches renderSparkline.
    G) initSparklines with data-neutral-band="0": falls back to nb=0
       (the `nb > 0` guard), same as A.

